# In depth documentation for Supabase migration from local SharedPreference

Current Application Structure
The Invoice Generator app currently uses SharedPreferences for local data storage with four primary models:
1. Company Info (singleton model)
2. Clients (collection)
3. Invoices (collection)
4. Catalog Items (collection)
5. Invoice Settings (configuration)
Current Model Analysis
1. Company Info Model
* File Location: lib/models/company_info.dart
* Structure: Singleton model (no explicit ID)
* Key Fields:
    * businessName (required)
    * currency (required)
    * enableTax (required)
    * taxRate (optional)
    * Address fields (country, addressLine1, city are required)
    * Contact fields (phone, email, website are optional)
    * Bank details (all optional)
    * logoPath (for company logo)
* Storage: JSON object in SharedPreferences with key 'company_info'
* Special Handling: Logo files are backed up to "logos_backup" in app documents directory
2. Client Model
* File Location: lib/models/client.dart
* ID Structure: clientId in format "CLxxx" (e.g., "CL001")
* ID Generation: Generated in ClientService.generateClientId() by finding highest existing ID and incrementing
* Key Fields:
    * name (required)
    * clientId (required)
    * type (required, 'organization' or 'person')
    * Contact and address fields (mostly optional)
    * Financial fields (currency, amount, outstandingAmount, dueAmount, etc.)
* Storage: Array of JSON objects in SharedPreferences with key 'clients'
* Current Limitations:
    * No check for existing invoices before client deletion
    * No explicit validation when directly setting client IDs
3. Catalog Item Model
* File Location: lib/models/catalog_item.dart
* ID Structure: Uses title as unique identifier
* Key Fields:
    * title (required, serves as ID)
    * amount (required)
    * quantity (required)
    * currency (default "USD")
    * usageInfo (tracks usage in invoices)
* Storage: Array of JSON objects in SharedPreferences with key 'catalog_items'
* Current Limitations:
    * No explicit check to prevent duplicate catalog item titles
    * Relies on title as unique identifier without enforcing uniqueness
4. Invoice Model
* File Location: lib/models/invoice.dart
* ID Structure: invoiceId in format "inv-xxx" (e.g., "inv-001")
* ID Generation: InvoiceService.generateInvoiceId() finds highest existing ID and increments
* Alternative ID: Supports custom ID formats through InvoiceSettingsService
* Key Fields:
    * invoiceId (required)
    * client (required, embedded Client object)
    * items (required, array of CatalogItem objects)
    * issueDate and dueDate (required)
    * status (enum: overdue, outstanding, paid)
    * Financial fields (subtotal, taxRate, taxAmount, total)
    * templateName (default "Orange")
* Storage: Array of JSON objects in SharedPreferences with key 'invoices'
5. Invoice Settings
* File Location: lib/services/invoice_settings_service.dart
* Key Fields:
    * idFormat
    * customNotes
    * isAutoGenerate
    * idPrefix (default "INV")
    * lastInvoiceNumber
* Storage: JSON object in SharedPreferences with key 'invoice_settings'
Current Data Relationships and Integrity
1. Client to Invoice Relationship
* Type: One-to-many (one client can have many invoices)
* Reference Mechanism: Invoices contain full embedded Client object
* Data Integrity:
    * When client is updated, ClientService.updateClient() calls InvoiceService.updateClientInInvoices()
    * Client statistics are updated based on related invoices
* Current Limitations:
    * No check for existing invoices before client deletion
    * Client deletion can leave orphaned invoices
2. Catalog Item to Invoice Relationship
* Type: Many-to-many (multiple catalog items in multiple invoices)
* Reference Mechanism: Invoices contain embedded CatalogItem objects
* Data Integrity:
    * When catalog item is updated, CatalogService.updateItem() calls _updateCatalogItemInInvoices()
    * When catalog item is deleted, CatalogService.deleteItem() calls InvoiceService.handleDeletedCatalogItem()
    * Items are automatically removed from invoices with recalculation of totals (CASCADE behavior)
    * CatalogItem usage statistics are updated based on invoice references
3. Statistics and Background Updates
* Mechanism: Background processes for statistics updates
* Methods:
    * InvoiceService._updateStatisticsInBackground()
    * InvoiceService._updateStatisticsForInvoiceChangesInBackground()
    * InvoiceService._updateStatisticsForDeletedInvoiceInBackground()
* Circular Updates Prevention: Methods like updateClientSilently() and updateItemSilently() prevent circular update cascades
4. Transaction Handling and Error Recovery
* Current Implementation:
    * Try-catch blocks simulate transaction rollback on error
    * No atomic guarantees for operations spanning multiple entities
    * Sequential operations update primary entity first, then related entities
    * Risk of inconsistent state if operations fail partially
5. Performance Considerations
* Current Lookups:
    * O(n) linear scans for client lookups
    * O(n) filtering of invoices by status
    * No indexing for searches or filtering
* Data Duplication:
    * Full embedding of client data in invoices increases storage but improves read performance
    * Increases risk of data inconsistency when updating
